Development notes
=================

Build and test with the maintained top-level Makefile:

    make
    make lib
    make test

The build uses the checked-in config.h and does not require autotools,
configure, automake, or libtool.

Library layout
==============

The public API is declared in include/lame.h. Most encoder implementation
code lives in libmp3lame/.

The main frontend entry point is frontend/main.c. It is a command line
consumer of libmp3lame and is useful as an API usage example.

mpglib/ contains MP3 decoder support used by libmp3lame. The static library
target folds those objects into libmp3lame/libmp3lame.a so consumers only need
to link one archive.

Adding options
==============

For a new encoder setting:

1. Add storage to the relevant encoder state.
2. Add setter and getter functions in libmp3lame/set_get.c if it is public API.
3. Declare public API only in include/lame.h.
4. Add command line parsing in frontend/parse.c when the frontend should expose it.
5. Update USAGE and the long help text in frontend/parse.c.

Keep experimental frontend-only helpers out of include/lame.h.
